+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running Sagan
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Sagan is configured in ${SYSCONFDIR}/sagan.yaml.  An example configuration
is installed as:

	${TRUEPREFIX}/share/examples/sagan/sagan.yaml

Copy it into place and adjust it to your needs:

	# cp ${TRUEPREFIX}/share/examples/sagan/sagan.yaml ${SYSCONFDIR}/sagan.yaml

Sagan does not ship any rules.  Download a ruleset (for example from
https://github.com/quadrantsec/sagan-rules) and point $RULE_PATH at it.

Sagan reads events from a FIFO.  By default the example configuration
uses:

	${LOCALSTATEDIR}/sagan/fifo/sagan.fifo

Feed it from your syslog daemon.  For example, with syslog-ng:

	destination sagan {
		pipe("${LOCALSTATEDIR}/sagan/fifo/sagan.fifo"
		    template("$SOURCEIP|$FACILITY|$PRIORITY|$LEVEL|$TAG|"
		    "$YEAR-$MONTH-$DAY|$HOUR:$MIN:$SEC|$PROGRAM| $MSG\n")
		    template-escape(no));
	};
	log { source(s_sys); destination(sagan); };

The rc.d script is installed and enabled with:

	# rcctl enable sagan
	# rcctl start sagan

Sagan runs as the _sagan user.  Its log, pid file and memory mapped IPC
files live in /var/log/sagan, /var/run/sagan and ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/sagan/mmap.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Memory mapped IPC files
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Sagan pre-allocates large, mostly sparse files under
${LOCALSTATEDIR}/sagan/mmap to keep track of flexbits, thresholds, afters
and xbits.  Their size grows with the $MMAP_DEFAULT variable in sagan.yaml.

For performance you can back this directory with memory, for example:

	# tmpfs ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/sagan/mmap mfs rw,-s32m 0 0

or, without an fstab entry:

	# mount_mfs -s 32m swap ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/sagan/mmap

Note that these files are what lets Sagan remember flexbit, threshold and
after state across restarts.  A memory backed ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/sagan/mmap
loses that state on reboot, so only use it if you do not need persistence.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Optional features
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

The port builds with GeoIP and Redis support disabled by default.  Enable
them by selecting the matching flavor when building the package:

	FLAVOR=geoip	# Maxmind GeoIP2 support
	FLAVOR=redis	# Redis as a flexbit storage backend

GeoIP requires a GeoLite2 database, configured via the "country_database"
option in the geoip section of sagan.yaml.  Redis requires a running Redis
server, configured via the redis-server section.
